d against the Wave-1 unanimous direction — that AI-Q3 is a quantity question gated by interconnection queues, transformers and licensed electricians rather than a financing question gated by the term premium, so a higher cost of capital changes who owns and who writes down the asset, not the megawatts. The converse observation (Q3 below 900 TWh with impairments above 20%) would falsify it and restore the Wave-1 coupling direction, moving my coupling note's Q3 call from flat-to-up back to down and raising the weight I place on the loanable-funds channel in r* from +5bp toward +15bp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of >=25% occurs and G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yields fall by >=100bp from the equity peak date to the trough date — the bond hedge works emphatically, not marginally — while the trailing MOVE average since Jan 2027 is still below 100.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Consumes CQ5's most likely qualifying episode with a non-qualifying case and confirms the Wave-1 disinflationary-bust premise against the red-team's credit-event argument that I partly accepted. CQ5 falls from 28 to ~13 (short remaining window, both conjuncts weakened simultaneously). It also implies abundant precautionary saving, so CQ4 P50 falls ~30bp and my repression branch probability falls from 0.38 toward 0.28 (a sovereign that still rallies in stress needs no policy backstop); CQ6-D rises from 13 to ~18 at B's and C's expense.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'rstar'."}}